      "writtenOn": "2020-12-14T02:42:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Dear Yujing Gu,I have 2 question for above conversations.\n\n1. I think you and Nan Zhao have a different understanding of multiple Email/Anr. Could you plz see the table G.1: Structure of EFs inside DF phonebook in spec doc. - ts 131.102 Annex G: Phonebook Example?  If one SIM supports 2 Phonebook sets for EFEMAIL, EFEMAILA (0x4f50) and EFEMAILB (0x4f51), then how does Android decide the length of vec\u003cstring\u003e emails using PhonebookCapacity?\nI agree with Nan Zhao\u0027s idea. PhonebookCapacity needs 2 new items to mark how many email/anr supported by the SIM card.\n\n2. For your RIL interface, how can Android know EFAAS info for each additionalNumber?\nIf not, I think PhonebookRecordInfo needs new item which indicates EFAAS.\n\nstruct PhonebookRecordInfo {\n\n    /** Additional numbers */\n    vec\u003cstring\u003e additionalNumbers;\n\n    /** Additional number Alpha Strings */\n    vec\u003cstring\u003e additionalNumberAlphaStrings;",
      "parentUuid": "2050500a_8d40b28d",
      "revId": "8eb72b136cf4dd5328428536c7de20111b100cd3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "88384dd6_d8acf861",
        "filename": "radio/1.6/types.hal",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 350,
