      "message": "Yes. I have one SIM card which has 2 EF_ANR file under EF_PBR.\n01-13 16:16:22.644  5556  5556 D UsimPhoneBookManager #0: PBR rec: \nA8 23\n C0 03 4F3A 02 // EF_ADN\n C4 03 4F60 07 //0xC4 is EF_ANR_TAG - it is defined in UsimPhoneBookManager.java\n C4 03 4F64 08 // EF_ANR\n C1 03 4F84 0A // EF_IAP\n C6 03 4F80 05 // EF_GRP\n C9 03 4F20 0E // EF_UID\n C5 03 4F50 04 // EF_PBC\nA9 05 \n CA 03 4F70 09 // EF_EMAIL (type 2)\nAA 0F\n C8 03 4F4C 03\n C2 03 4F4A 06\n C7 03 4F4B 01\nFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF\n\nAnyway, I saw your last comment in https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/hardware/interfaces/+/1441011/5..12/radio/1.6/types.hal#b347. I think your way can be solution of multiple Email/Anr file case, although I still think it is better to have a variable indicating the number of supported Email/ANR file in SIM.",
